Node.js 24.4 or newer.

Install: npm ci --ignore-scripts
Local preview: npm run dev
Production server: npm run build, then npm start
Verification: npm test && npm run typecheck && npm run build
Public repository check: npm run check:public

Optional server settings are described in .env.example. Put real values in an
ignored .env.local for local development or in your hosting provider's secret
manager. Never use a NEXT_PUBLIC variable for provider URLs or keys.

Wallet queries use same-origin POST requests. The application does not persist
wallet queries, use browser storage, add addresses to URLs, or log request bodies,
provider responses, error stacks, or credentials. Hosting providers may maintain
infrastructure access logs; configure those independently and disable body tracing.

Historical scans are resumable and bounded. Keep SCAN_CURSOR_SECRET stable across
server instances for cursor continuity. Results are taken at a fixed confirmed
block and discarded if its hash changes. An incomplete scan never means zero fees.

Coverage in this first release: O1 current, Tax and historical fee escrows; the
shared Long/Longbow locked-pool manager; pons v2 fee escrow plus curve/hook discovery;
pons v1 lockers. Migrated Doppler pools and separate Long hook payouts are outside
coverage. Each source reports its exclusions and scan progress in the interface.

Wallet connection uses account access only, with Rabby preferred. Scanning never
requests a transaction. Each available fee has a separately reviewed claim action;
wallet approval is required for every transaction, with zero native value and no
token approval. Claims enforce Robinhood Chain, the connected fee recipient,
pinned contract code and simulation before submission. Pool claims collect both
currencies. Unswept estimates have no claim action.

Claim preparation and confirmation endpoints only perform reads. The browser
submits through the connected wallet. Failed send requests with an unknown outcome
are never resent automatically. Transaction status stays in memory; check wallet
activity before reloading if a submission's outcome is uncertain.

After mining, receipt checks verify the sender, target, exact calldata, native
value, canonical block and payout events. Refresh waits for 20 subsequent blocks,
then reuses a signed snapshot that includes the claim for balances and history.
A reverted or unverified payout is never recorded as a successful fee claim.

Account changes invalidate unsubmitted reviews. A submitted claim is still tracked
for its original owner; it only refreshes that owner's current view. Disconnecting
clears scan results. No wallet address, query, review or transaction history is
persisted by the application or written to logs.
Run git config core.hooksPath .githooks to enable local pre-commit guards.
